.\" Manpage for sxalert

.TH man 8 "19 Sept 2026" "0.2" "sxalert manual page"
.SH NAME
sxalert \- Simple X Alert
.SH SYNOPSIS
sxalert [OPTIONS] "First line" "Second line" "Third line"
.SH DESCRIPTION
sxalert will draw text as a notification for X

.SH OPTIONS

-t text color in hex

-g background color in hex

-r border color in hex

-b border width in pixels

-d duration in milliseconds
   for values below or equal to 0 the notification will run indefinitely

-h print help panel & exit

-v print version & exit

.SH EXIT CODES
0 - Left click on the notification window
1 - Midde click on the notification window
2 - Right click on the notification window
3 - Time out

.SH EXAMPLES

This will print the string "Updates available":

sxalert "Updates avalailable"

The following will also print "Updates available" but will specify text
color to be red, background to be black and border width to be 0:

sxlaert -t 0xff0000 -g 0x000000 -b 0 "Updates available"

These will overwrite the defaults specified in config.h

The following will print "New mail" and echo "OK" to stdout if the user
left clicks on the notification window:

sxalert "New mail" && echo "OK"

